--- body ---
## Context

0023 resolved the distribution model: the binary is the primary
artifact, and repo-local assets are managed by explicit bootstrap
commands rather than a separate installer script.

`erg init [DIR]` should materialize the repo support files from assets
embedded in the binary. `erg uninstall [DIR]` should remove only the
assets and file fragments managed by `erg`, leaving user ticket data in
place by default.

## Actions

1. Embed the bootstrap assets in the Go binary:
   - `tickets/README.md`
   - `tickets/spec-erg-v1.md`
   - `tickets/integration/**`
   - `tickets/tools/go/**` if vendored source remains part of repo init
2. Add `erg init [DIR]`:
   - Default `DIR` to `.`
   - Create/refresh the managed files under `tickets/`
   - Append the one-line `AGENTS.md` pointer if absent
   - Append the pre-commit hook block if absent
   - Add the `.gitignore` line for `tickets/tools/go/erg` if absent
   - Print a concise plan before mutating, then a summary of applied
     changes
3. Make `erg init` idempotent:
   - no duplicate hook block
   - no duplicate `AGENTS.md` line
   - repeat runs refresh managed files without duplicating fragments
4. Record enough metadata to support uninstall and safe refresh:
   - managed-file manifest and/or stable markers for appended fragments
5. Add `erg uninstall [DIR]`:
   - remove managed fragments from `AGENTS.md`, `.gitignore`, and
     `.git/hooks/pre-commit`
   - remove managed integration files and support files written by init
   - preserve user-created ticket files by default
6. Add tests covering init, re-init, and uninstall round-trip in a
   temp git repo

## Exit criteria

- [ ] `erg init .` bootstraps a clean repo from the binary alone
- [ ] `erg init .` is idempotent
- [ ] `erg uninstall .` removes only `erg`-managed assets/fragments
- [ ] User ticket data remains intact after uninstall by default
- [ ] Round-trip tests pass
